# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the real values — `.env` itself is
# gitignored (see .gitignore) so the real key never gets committed.
#
# Deliberately kept at the REPO ROOT rather than inside
# src/simulator-app/ — Vite only auto-loads .env files from an app's own
# root, and Vite additionally only exposes vars to client code if they're
# prefixed VITE_ (see https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html#env-files).
# Neither applies here on purpose: until the node server mentioned below
# exists, nothing should read this key from browser-bundled code at all —
# a Finnhub key embedded in the client JS is visible to anyone who opens
# devtools, defeating the point of keeping it server-side. This file is
# just a landing spot for local dev until that server reads it itself
# (e.g. via `dotenv`, from its own working directory).

# https://finnhub.io/docs/api — read by src/data-server, never directly by
# src/simulator-app's client-side code. NOT required for real candle
# data any more: that comes from Coinbase Exchange's public API instead
# (no key needed at all - see src/data-server/src/index.ts's top-of-file
# comment for why). This key is only used by data-server's /diagnose and
# /quote routes now, which are diagnostic/reference only - leave this
# blank and everything except those two routes still works.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Finnhub's webhook secret — validates the `X-Finnhub-Secret` header on
# incoming webhook requests once the node server exposes an endpoint for
# them. Also server-side only.
FINNHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
